## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project.

### Changes Made

**Installed Package:**
- Added `@vercel/analytics` via npm
- Package version installed: latest available

**Modified Files:**
1. `next-app/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
2. `next-app/package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
3. `next-app/src/app/layout.tsx` - Integrated Analytics component

**Code Changes in layout.tsx:**
- Imported Analytics component from '@vercel/analytics/next'
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after {children}
- Preserved all existing code structure and functionality

### Implementation Details

This is an App Router project (detected by the presence of `src/app/layout.tsx`), so the Analytics component was added to the root layout file as specified in Vercel's documentation.

The Analytics component is placed at the end of the body tag to ensure it loads after the main content, following best practices for analytics integration.

### Verification

✅ Build completed successfully - no build errors
✅ TypeScript compilation passed
✅ Dependencies installed correctly
✅ Lock file updated (package-lock.json)

**Note:** The linter reported errors in pre-existing code (src/components/index.tsx), which are unrelated to this Analytics implementation. These errors existed before this change and should be addressed separately.

### Next Steps

The Analytics will automatically start collecting data when this application is deployed to Vercel. No additional configuration is required unless you want to customize the analytics behavior.
